WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.003
-Democrats are debating whether
to move forward with impeachment

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.873
as President Trump awaits orders
from Saudi Arabia.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.875
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:13.480
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.947
Well, it's campaign season,

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.450
which means we'll all be
subjected to endless hours

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.786
of cable news speculation about
every morsel of political news,

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:23.656
from every poll result
to every fundraising report,

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.226
with panels of truly absurd
numbers of people

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.928
sitting around giant tables,
endlessly dissecting

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.830
who's up and who's down
in the race.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.964
And I'm sorry,
but what is up with

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.634
this weird horseshoe
configuration?

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.936
You couldn't find a table
that looks less like

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.238
the Legion of Doom?

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.006
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.374
This is, of course,
the time of year

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.843
when the cable news pundits
speculate wildly,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.844
and often wrongly.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.245
For example,
you might remember that,

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:47.813
when Elizabeth Warren

00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:50.016
announced that she was
exploring a presidential run

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.918
at end of 2018,
many pundits

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.719
proclaimed her candidacy
dead on arrival

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.121
because she had supposedly
missed her moment

00:00:56.121 --> 00:00:57.723
by not running
four years ago.

00:00:57.723 --> 00:00:59.625
-As Elizabeth Warren
inches towards

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:01.828
a possible presidential run
in 2020,

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.363
President Trump
is laughing her off.

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:07.800
Does she stand a chance,
or has she missed her moment?

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.602
-In a new editorial,
the<i> Boston Globe</i> writing,

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.405
quote, "Warren missed her moment
in 2016,

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.973
and there's reason
to be skeptical

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.275
of her perspective candidacy
in 2020."

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:19.011
-There are some say that
she missed her shot

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:21.213
to run in 2016
for president.

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:24.183
-Perhaps 2016 was
Elizabeth Warren's moment,

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:25.484
and she should have
run then.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:31.090
-In 2016, she had so many people
urging her to run.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.725
-She might have missed
her moment.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.160
That might have been
her moment.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:39.566
-She maybe missed her moment,
in some eyes, back in 2016.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.534
-You know your
political analysis is bad

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.537
when you sound like you're
quoting a Kelly Clarkson song.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.071
"You know what?
She missed her moment.

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:49.075
And a moment like this,
some people wait a lifetime

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:52.144
for a moment like this."

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:54.380
Also, can we go back to
this part, real quick.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.649
-As Elizabeth Warren inches
towards a possible

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.351
presidential run
in 2020,

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:01.187
President Trump
is laughing her off.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.456
I'm sorry,
Trump is laughing her off?

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.891
If laughing at somebody meant
they couldn't be president,

00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:08.327
then, we sure as hell wouldn't
have Trump to deal with.

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:11.163
Donald Trump often appears
on Fox, which is ironic,

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:13.866
because a fox often appears
on Donald Trump's head.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.136
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.507
By the way, that...

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:22.508
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.979
...interesting factoid --

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.281
that comedian, right there,
that's my son.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:31.584
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.785
But anyway,
there you go.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.187
The pundits said
Elizabeth Warren

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.655
missed her moment.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:37.489
And if there is one thing we've
learned from the last decade

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:40.293
of politics, it's that
the pundits are always right.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.696
-Momentum growing for a surging
Senator Elizabeth Warren.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:47.467
-Senator Elizabeth Warren
surging in this latest poll.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.669
-Warren is surging.
-She is surging.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.471
All eyes are on
a surging Elizabeth Warren.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:55.475
-New polling shows
Warren's economic message

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.110
is resonating
with voters.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.078
-Take a look at thousands --
thousands of people

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.614
who gathered in New York City's
Washington Square Park

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:04.383
last night for Warren's
anti-corruption speech.

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:06.653
-Her campaign said
the presidential candidate

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:10.289
drew a crowd
of 20,000 people to her rally

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:11.557
in New York City
last night --

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:14.027
the biggest crowd
of her campaign so far.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.295
-Warren vowed
to take a selfie

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:18.631
with everyone who wanted one
at the end.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:21.567
So, that selfie line
for a crowd of 20,000

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.570
lasted for four hours.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.737
-Wow.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.306
-She stood there and took
selfies after her speech

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.340
for four hours.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.876
Can you imagine Trump
doing that?

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:35.280
I mean, look at how much
he sweats during his speeches.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.818
You know you're out of shape
when talking is cardio.

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:43.623
After four hours of selfies,
he'd just be a puddle with hair.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.494
But Warren's speech
was not just...

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:51.463
was not just about
showcasing enthusiasm

00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:52.732
or posing for selfies.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.600
It was also about hitting home
a crucial point --

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.235
a distinction she has drawn

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:58.370
with one of her main rivals,
Joe Biden.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.105
Biden has basically said that,
once Trump is gone,

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:01.374
things will go
back to normal.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.109
Warren, on the other hand,
has stressed

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:05.411
that Trump is both the product
and the symbol

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.645
of a broken system.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:10.917
-Now, when you see a government
that works great

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.120
for those with money
and connections,

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.323
and doesn't work
for much of anyone else,

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.859
that's corruption,
plain and simple,

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:22.128
and we need to call it out
for what it is.

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:23.496
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:27.166
Okay. So, let's start
with the obvious.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:30.236
Donald Trump is corruption
in the flesh.

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:31.603
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:31.603 --> 00:04:35.941
Now, as bad as things are,
we have to recognize

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:39.245
our problems didn't start
with Donald Trump.

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:42.748
He made them worse, but we need
to take a deep breath,

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:46.985
and recognize that a country
that elects Donald Trump

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:49.855
is already
in serious trouble.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:51.290
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.825
-That's a very good point.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.495
It's like finding out your
daughter is dating a deejay --

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.463
getting rid of the deejay
is fine,

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.865
but you still have to
go back and examine

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:01.601
the way you raised
your daughter.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:05.904
"What did we do?"

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:07.540
Also, can we
go back to this.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.710
-Donald Trump is corruption
in the flesh.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.644
-The only part of that
I disagree with

00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:15.147
is the idea that Trump
has actual human flesh.

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:16.683
I mean, look at him.

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:19.518
His actual face
is indistinguishable

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:20.887
from a Halloween mask.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.621
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:24.490
Anyway, the rest of the point
still stands.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:25.991
Trump is the symbol
and the product

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:29.195
of years of elite failure and
institutionalized corruption --

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:31.730
a system which Trump
has both benefited from

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:32.932
and made worse.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:35.001
Even if you put aside
the mountains of evidence

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.668
in the 400-page
Mueller report,

00:05:36.668 --> 00:05:39.238
and all of the obvious ways in
which he's using the presidency

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.240
to enrich himself,
this week, Trump threatened

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.942
an illegal and unconstitutional
war with Iran

00:05:43.942 --> 00:05:46.745
because Saudi Arabia
pays us money.

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:49.382
-We would certainly
help them.

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.850
They've been
a great ally.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:55.054
They spent $400 billion
in our country

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.455
over the last number
of years.

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:57.856
$400 billion.

00:05:57.856 --> 00:06:01.627
That's a million
and a half jobs.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:03.829
And they're not ones that,
unlike some countries,

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:04.897
where they want terms.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:06.398
They want terms
and conditions.

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:09.368
They want to say "Can we borrow
the money at 0% for

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:10.536
the next 400 years."

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:13.072
No. No.
Saudi Arabia pays cash.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:16.342
-Wait. They paid you
$400 billion in cash?

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:18.444
How does anyone --

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.580
I think they're
scamming you, dude.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:25.317
[ As Trump ] They gave me
$400 billion dollar bills.

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:26.452
And you know they're real,

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:29.955
because they had Ivanka
on them.

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:31.790
[ Normal voice ] And of course,
as we've established

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.759
on this show repeatedly,
Trump has all kinds

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:35.694
of personal financial ties
from Saudi Arabia,

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:37.463
from which he has
personally profited

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.332
both before and during
his presidency.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:42.401
At one point, he literally said
straight up during the campaign

00:06:42.401 --> 00:06:45.470
that he likes Saudi Arabia
because they give him money.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.773
-I love the Saudis.
Many are in this building.

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:50.509
Saudi Arabia, and I get along
great with all of them.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:51.811
They buy apartments
from me.

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:53.679
They spend $40 million,
$50 million.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:54.713
Am I supposed
to dislike them?

00:06:54.713 --> 00:06:56.716
I like them very much.

00:06:56.716 --> 00:07:00.219
-That is the literal
definition of a bribe.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:02.121
And this is the problem
with Trump --

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.791
he just confessed openly,
in plain sight,

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:06.425
in front of the cameras,
microphones on,

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:08.260
so it doesn't feel like
a confession.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:11.564
But just imagine that same quote
in a different context.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.499
Trump's in a police
interrogation room

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:16.035
with Lennie Briscoe, and it's
hour six of the interview,

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:18.571
light swinging over his head,
sweat pouring down his face,

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:19.705
and the cops are screaming,

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.407
"Tell us what you know
about the Saudis!"

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:24.142
And Trump's like, "Fine.
They buy apartments from me --

00:07:24.142 --> 00:07:25.677
$40 million,
$50 million.

00:07:25.677 --> 00:07:28.247
Am I supposed to dislike them?
I like them very much.

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:31.817
Oh, God what I have said."

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:34.086
Since then, we've learned that
Trump has registered companies

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:36.455
in Saudi Arabia,
and Saudi officials and lobbyist

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:37.789
spend money at his hotels.

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:39.658
In fact, this week,
we got yet another example

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:42.361
of Saudi Arabia spending money
at Trump's personal properties,

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:45.130
when Politico reported that
a large group of Saudi royals

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.666
had stayed at Trump's
golf resort in Scotland

00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:48.934
earlier this summer.

00:07:48.934 --> 00:07:51.303
According to a staffer,
a group of Saudi royals

00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:53.139
stayed at the resort
for about a week

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:55.073
at the tail end
of extended travel,

00:07:55.073 --> 00:07:56.675
bringing a party
of 25 people

00:07:56.675 --> 00:07:58.677
and more than 100
pieces of luggage.

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:00.679
100 pieces of luggage.

00:08:00.679 --> 00:08:03.349
You know, one bag for clothes,
one bag for golf clubs,

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:06.519
and 98 bags
stuffed with gold bars.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:08.487
I'm just kidding.
They would never bring gold.

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:10.589
-Saudi Arabia pays cash.

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:14.993
-This is a kind of corruption
that is been institutionalized

00:08:14.993 --> 00:08:16.395
in Washington
for years.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:17.997
It's just that Trump
came along,

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:19.932
and made it worse,
and more obvious.

00:08:19.932 --> 00:08:22.368
It's also blatantly illegal
and unconstitutional,

00:08:22.368 --> 00:08:25.204
which is why more and more
Democrats are coming around

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:26.872
to the idea that Trump
should be impeached.

00:08:26.872 --> 00:08:29.541
And yet, once again, the pundits
and the establishment

00:08:29.541 --> 00:08:31.676
who predicted that Warren
had missed her moment

00:08:31.676 --> 00:08:33.078
are now hand-wringing

00:08:33.078 --> 00:08:35.247
about the possible political
consequences impeachment --

00:08:35.247 --> 00:08:38.017
like this item from Politico,
explaining the thinking

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:39.952
of Democratic leaders
on impeachment.

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:42.988
Try to follow along, and see if
any of this makes sense to you.

00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:45.657
"This political pickle
has come up in conversations

00:08:45.657 --> 00:08:48.160
with several Democratic sources
over the last few days.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.662
If House Democrats impeach
President Donald Trump,

00:08:50.662 --> 00:08:53.499
and he loses, they fear
they could get blamed

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:54.633
for a political hit job.

00:08:54.633 --> 00:08:56.502
If they don't impeach him,
and he wins,

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:58.970
they fear being blamed
by the Democratic base

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.172
for not doing enough.

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.808
Best-case scenario,
Dems are left hoping

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:05.611
they don't impeach him,
and Trump loses on his own.

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:07.947
-First of all, that is not
the best-case scenario.

00:09:07.947 --> 00:09:10.849
The best-case scenario is that
Trump sets his Diet Coke down

00:09:10.849 --> 00:09:12.884
on his computer,
and accidentally sends

00:09:12.884 --> 00:09:15.087
all his texts with Putin
to the<i> New York Times.</i>

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:18.190
Then, he has to flee to Mexico,
but he gets his pants stuck

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.958
climbing over his
newly built wall,

00:09:19.958 --> 00:09:22.928
and falls bare-assed
on the Mexican side,

00:09:22.928 --> 00:09:26.365
and that photograph is the only
thing on CNN for, like, a year.

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:27.533
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:30.036
That is the
best-case scenario.

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:31.771
[ Applause ]

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:35.340
Second, the same pundits
who speculated wildly

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.709
about Warren
missing her moment

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:38.777
are the same ones
now insisting that impeaching

00:09:38.777 --> 00:09:41.447
a lawless, corrupt President
could hurt Democrats.

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:43.248
Who knows what will happen
in either case,

00:09:43.248 --> 00:09:44.683
but several things
are clear --

00:09:44.683 --> 00:09:46.952
Trump has broken the law,
violated the Constitution,

00:09:46.952 --> 00:09:48.286
and, judging from
his rallies,

00:09:48.286 --> 00:09:50.622
he has got some very
serious problems, especially...

00:09:50.622 --> 00:09:52.191
-In the flesh.

00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:53.892
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:09:53.892 --> 00:09:58.397
[ Cheers and applause ]

